From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] board: qualcomm: iceland: Pass ABL's boot mode (charger) on
 to the OS

With a USB cable in, a powered-off Pad 4 is powered on again by VBUS.
ABL then starts the boot partition in its off-mode charging mode (stock:
Android's charging screen) and says so in the DT it hands over:
"androidboot.mode=charger" in the bootconfig block at the end of the
ramdisk (boot image header v4; header v3 and older: in bootargs), and,
on OnePlus ABLs, "oplusboot.mode=<mode>" in /chosen bootargs (normal,
reboot, charger, ...; the stock kernel's oplus_bsp_bootmode parses it).
U-Boot boots its OS itself over EFI, so the OS never sees any of this:
Fedora came up with its desktop on every cable power-on.

Read the three sources once, early in board_late_init() (before U-Boot
loads anything into RAM), from ABL's DT (get_prev_bl_fdt_addr()):
bootargs, and the bootconfig block found through /chosen
linux,initrd-start / -end (trailer as the kernel reads it: size,
byte-sum checksum, "#BOOTCONFIG\n", up to 3 bytes of padding). Only
memory inside U-Boot's DRAM banks is read. A value is used only if it
is [a-z0-9_-]{1,15}. "charger" from any source wins; otherwise the
first source that has a value; otherwise "unknown".

The result goes into ${abl_boot_mode}, one console line ("ABL boot
mode: ...", readable with `fastboot oem console`), and the OS's DT:
ft_board_setup() adds /chosen u-boot,abl-boot-mode (the mode) and
u-boot,abl-boot-mode-source (what each source said). The EFI boot
manager applies ft_board_setup() to the DT it loads from the ESP, so
Linux finds the mode in /proc/device-tree/chosen/.

Read only: nothing is written but U-Boot's environment and the OS's DT.
Every failure is logged and ignored; the boot itself is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/Kconfig         |  11 +
 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/Makefile        |   1 +
 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/abl-boot-mode.h |  20 ++
 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/abl_boot_mode.c | 331 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/board.c         |   4 +
 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/of_fixup.c      |   5 +
 configs/iceland_defconfig                |   1 +
 7 files changed, 373 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/abl-boot-mode.h
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/abl_boot_mode.c

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/Kconfig b/arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/Kconfig
index d3de8693..9dd0fdf7 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/Kconfig
@@ -42,4 +42,15 @@ config SYS_CONFIG_NAME
 	  Based on this option include/configs/<CONFIG_SYS_CONFIG_NAME>.h header
 	  will be used for board configuration.
 
+config QCOM_ABL_BOOT_MODE
+	bool "Pass the Android boot loader's boot mode on to the OS"
+	depends on OF_LIBFDT && OF_BOARD_SETUP && OF_LIVE
+	help
+	  Read the boot mode the previous boot loader (ABL) put into the DT
+	  it handed over (oplusboot.mode= / androidboot.mode= in /chosen
+	  bootargs, androidboot.mode in the bootconfig block at the end of
+	  its ramdisk), store it in ${abl_boot_mode} and add it to the OS's
+	  /chosen as u-boot,abl-boot-mode. Read only. Lets the OS tell an
+	  off-mode charging start (USB cable power-on) from a normal one.
+
 endif
